 * applicable / an exception, the reference to the work done, a note, then the area's conclusion and the preparer's and
 * reviewer's sign-off). Step 14 of the work on a client (App\Services\Audit\AuditProcedures).
 *
 * An area: its paper code, its title, the statement lines whose balance it audits (to show the balance and whether it is at or
 * above the performance materiality), and its procedures. A procedure: [text, assertions, type]. Its key («01», «02» …) is
 * what the accountant's answers are kept under: add new procedures at the END of an area, never renumber one.
 *
 * An area also names what it rests on: `requirements` (the documents asked of the client, config/audit_requirements.php: a
 * section, or «section::word» for that section's requests whose title holds the word), `papers` (the working papers and the
 * recalculations the client fills: the request's `paper` key), `standards` (the ISAs it applies) and `framework` (the IFRS for
 * SMEs sections of the balances it audits).
 *
 * Types: general (planning and completion), analytical (analytical procedures), control (tests of controls), detail (tests of
 * details), sample (a test of details on a sample: the page links it to step 13).
 * Assertions (ISA 315): existence, occurrence, completeness, accuracy, valuation, rights (rights and obligations), cutoff,
 * classification, presentation (presentation and disclosure).
 */
